## after: settings claude --global, outside any project
Put these settings in <scratch>/claude-home/settings.json, merged with any already there.
They set up every project at once, and do nothing in a project with no
.handoff/ or a session with no role. Sessions already running get them
when they start again.
In a project with a record, every Claude Code session takes the role you give
it: tell it, and it runs handoff role <role>. Until then it has none. It gets
the brief when it starts or is summarised, a hook listens for its work
whenever its turn ends, and it runs handoff without asking, but never decides,
nor edits a .handoff/ folder.

{
  "hooks": {
    "Notification": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "args": [
              "hook",
              "notify"
            ],
            "command": "handoff",
            "type": "command"
          }
        ],
        "matcher": "permission_prompt"
      }
    ],
    "SessionStart": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "args": [
              "hook",
              "brief"
            ],
            "command": "handoff",
            "type": "command"
          },
          {
            "args": [
              "hook",
              "listen"
            ],
            "asyncRewake": true,
            "command": "handoff",
            "timeout": 86400,
            "type": "command"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "Stop": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "args": [
              "hook",
              "listen"
            ],
            "asyncRewake": true,
            "command": "handoff",
            "timeout": 86400,
            "type": "command"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "permissions": {
    "allow": [
      "Bash(handoff *)"
    ],
    "deny": [
      "Bash(handoff decide *)",
      "Edit(//**/.handoff/**)"
    ]
  }
}
# exit 0
## after: settings codex --global, outside any project
Put these two files in <scratch>/codex-home/, merged with any already there.
They set up every project at once, and do nothing in a project with no
.handoff/ or a session with no role. The next time Codex starts, it asks you
to review the new hooks: choose Trust all. Sessions already running get them
when they start again.
In a project with a record, every Codex session takes the role you give it:
tell it, and it runs handoff role <role>. Until then it has none, and handoff
on its own never shows it your decisions. It gets the brief when its first
turn starts and after a summary. When its turn would end, a hook listens for
its work and continues it with what arrives. And handoff runs outside Codex's
sandbox, so its notifications and pop-ups reach you; handoff decide is
forbidden.

<scratch>/codex-home/hooks.json:
{
  "hooks": {
    "SessionStart": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "command": "exec handoff hook brief",
            "timeout": 30,
            "type": "command"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "Stop": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "command": "exec handoff hook listen",
            "timeout": 86400,
            "type": "command"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}

<scratch>/codex-home/rules/handoff.rules:
# handoff writes only under .handoff/ and has no network code (proposal §9).
prefix_rule(pattern=["handoff"], decision="allow", justification="handoff runs outside the sandbox so that it can notify the operator")
prefix_rule(pattern=["handoff", "decide"], decision="forbidden", justification="The operator decides, not an agent")
# exit 0
handoff settings: --as fixes a role in one project; with --global, each session takes the role you give it
