## after: brief, in a Claude Code session
Listening: Run `handoff wait --for reviewer --timeout 25m` in the background. Exit 3: run it again. Exit 4: another session already listens for reviewer. After you handle what it delivers, wait again. If your session has no handoff hooks, offer to set them up for every project: `handoff settings claude --global` prints them and where they go. With the operator's OK, add them. They work once the operator starts this session again.
## after: brief, in a Codex session
Listening: Don't run `handoff wait`: Codex checks on a running command about once a minute, each time with a whole model call, which uses up the operator's plan. Instead, end your turn. If work waits for you, the operator hears of it and tells you. If your session has no handoff hooks, offer to set them up for every project: `handoff settings codex --global` prints them and where they go. With the operator's OK, add them. They work once the operator starts this session again.
## after: brief, outside a session
Listening: In Claude Code, run `handoff wait --for reviewer --timeout 25m` in the background. Exit 3: run it again. Exit 4: another session already listens for reviewer. After you handle what it delivers, wait again. In Codex, don't run wait, since each minute of it costs a whole model call: end your turn. If work waits for you, the operator hears of it and tells you. If your session has no handoff hooks, offer to set them up for every project: `handoff settings claude --global` or `handoff settings codex --global` prints them and where they go. With the operator's OK, add them. They work once the operator starts this session again.
## after: role, in a Claude Code session
Listening: if your session has handoff's hooks, a hook listens for implementer when your turn ends, and you don't run wait. If not, run `handoff wait --for implementer --timeout 25m` in the background. Exit 3: run it again. Exit 4: another session already listens for implementer. After you handle what it delivers, wait again. If your session has no handoff hooks, offer to set them up for every project: `handoff settings claude --global` prints them and where they go. With the operator's OK, add them. They work once the operator starts this session again.
## after: role, in a Codex session
Listening: if your session has handoff's hooks, a hook listens for reviewer-2 when your turn ends, and you don't run wait. If not, don't run `handoff wait`: Codex checks on a running command about once a minute, each time with a whole model call, which uses up the operator's plan. Instead, end your turn. If work waits for you, the operator hears of it and tells you. If your session has no handoff hooks, offer to set them up for every project: `handoff settings codex --global` prints them and where they go. With the operator's OK, add them. They work once the operator starts this session again.
